    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d633">

                <pb facs="0878" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg778"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7412 Amateur/4</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Mexican Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Torreblanca</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        American Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>)<anchor
                        n="21" xml:id="d633-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">[No.] 2098</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-05-14">May 14, 1934</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Chargé d’affaires</hi>: I refer to that
                    Embassy’s courteous note number 472 of March 29th last, in order to advise you
                    that the competent <pb facs="0879" n="779" xml:id="pg779"/> authorities have
                    informed this Ministry that they would view with great satisfaction the
                    conclusion of the agreement proposed by the American Government,<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d633-f2"/> relative to radio communication, on behalf of third
                    parties, between amateur stations of Mexico and the United States; but that, it
                    being impossible to do this under the terms of the laws in effect, the
                    authorities in question are considering the manner of broadening the
                    restrictions governing the matter with a view to rendering possible the
                    acceptance of the proposal of that Embassy.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Torreblanca</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d633-f1" n="21" type="source" xml:id="d633-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by The Chargé in Mexico in his despatch No.
                    1434, May 18; received May 22.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d633-f2" n="22" xml:id="d633-f2-content">
                <p>An agreement by an exchange of notes was suggested similar to the negotiations
                    between the United States and Canada in 1928 and 1929 (<ref
                        target="frus1929v02#pg_114">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1929, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, pp. 114</ref> ff).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
